 "attributes": {
  "title": {
   "en": "How Do I, and We Live?"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja-ro": "Boku wa, Soshite Bokutachi wa Dou Ikiru ka"
   },
   {
    "ja": "僕は、そして僕たちはどう生きるか"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "Minori Kimura has made a manga adaptation of Kaho Nashiki's masterpiece \"How Do I, and We, Live?\" (Rironsha, later Iwanami Gendai Bunko)! \"I\", a 14 year-old, is called \"Koperu\" after the main character of the novel \"How Do You Live?\" On the morning of the first day of the long weekend, his uncle Nobo, a dyer and weaver, comes to visit him and he decides to go and see his best friend Eugene, who has stopped going to school... Why don't we think together about the meaning of living without letting go of \"thinking\"?"
  },
